# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 13-accessibility-i18n-performance

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

ACCESSIBILITY EXPANSION (APP-A11Y-\*) — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-A11Y-WCAG-FLOOR [QA]

\- Where web content or standards applicability requires
it, target WCAG 2.2 AA.

\- Native platform accessibility requirements must also
be met.

\- Complements APP-UI-A11Y-FLOOR (44×44 dp, contrast,
Dynamic Type / Large Text).



APP-A11Y-SEMANTICS [QA]

\- Interactive controls must expose meaningful labels, roles,
states, and values to supported

  accessibility
services.



APP-A11Y-KEYBOARD [QA]

\- Desktop interfaces must support logical keyboard
navigation, visible focus, and activation of

  core actions
without requiring a pointer.



APP-A11Y-NO-COLOR-ONLY [QA]

\- Do not communicate required information, errors,
status, or actions through color alone.



APP-A11Y-TEXT-SCALING [QA]

\- Display Resolution Awareness & Full UI Scalability: Every application MUST be
display resolution aware and render sharply and correctly on high-resolution (HiDPI / 4K / Retina)
displays. Large text, system text scaling, display zoom percentage changes (100%, 125%, 150%, 175%,
200%, 250%, 300%+), and dynamic per-monitor DPI transitions must scale the entire application appropriately.

\- High-DPI Startup Contract: On desktop platforms, high-DPI awareness (e.g. PerMonitorV2) must be
explicitly declared at startup prior to any UI font or control creation, preventing low-DPI bitmap
blurriness and scaling distortion.

\- Critical controls, inputs, numeric spinners, dropdowns, buttons, sliders/trackbars, labels,
validation messages, and navigation must remain fully visible, readable, and operable without
text truncation, squashed heights, or clipping.

\- Fixed 96-DPI pixel heights and widths on interactive chrome are prohibited. Input heights and
bounds must adapt dynamically to font metrics and DPI scale factors (e.g. using preferred heights
or DPI-scaled dimensions).

\- Vector Glyphs & Assets: Render UI icons, history arrows, and visual markers as vector paths
or multi-density assets scaled to the active DPI rather than fixed unscaled raster bitmaps.

\- Grouped controls (such as a label, slider groove, and value readout) must be encapsulated to
wrap and move together as atomic units rather than fragmenting across line breaks.

\- Dialogs, help hubs, and legal gates must support dynamic font/DPI auto-scaling.



APP-UI-UNIFORM-SURFACE-VIEWPORT [GATE]

\- Desktop workstation apps with dense fixed layouts MUST follow
reference/NIVO78_UNIFORM_UI_SURFACE_AND_VIEWPORT.md: 1920×1080 logical surface, single
ScaleFactor, explicit main viewport scroll (CompactMainViewportHost — not primary
AutoScroll), scroll home flush top-left, signed wheel delta. Port from N78-Estimate; do
not rebuild per product. See also uniform-ui-surface-viewport.mdc.



APP-A11Y-MOTION [QA]

\- Nonessential animation must not interfere with
operation, and supported reduced-motion preferences

  should be
respected.





\================================================================================

INTERNATIONALIZATION AND LOCALIZATION (APP-I18N-\*) —
EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-I18N-NO-HARDCODED-UI [STATIC]

\- User-visible strings must be stored through the
platform/application localization mechanism rather

  than embedded
directly in business or UI logic where localization is expected.



APP-I18N-DATE-NUMBER [QA]

\- Dates, times, numbers, currencies, and units must
use explicit, locale-aware formatting where applicable.



APP-I18N-TEXT-EXPANSION [QA]

\- Layouts must tolerate reasonable text expansion
without clipping, overlap, or loss of required actions.



APP-I18N-RTL-READY [QA]

\- Shared UI architecture must avoid assumptions that
prevent right-to-left presentation if localization

  is added
later.





\================================================================================

PERFORMANCE (APP-PERF-\*) — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



APP-PERF-BUDGET [QA]

\- Each product must define reasonable performance
budgets for startup, core interaction responsiveness,

  memory,
storage, and—on mobile—battery impact, appropriate to the product's job.



APP-PERF-NO-BLOCKING-UI [STATIC]

\- Long-running calculations, file operations,
encryption, migrations, imports, exports, and network

  operations
must not unnecessarily block the UI thread.



APP-PERF-LARGE-DATA [QA]

\- Critical workflows must be tested with realistic
large datasets where the product can reasonably

  accumulate
substantial data.

